Z||000003||Tigger||11-28-2000||01:30 PM||||When I bought mine, I found the stock '84 fan motor had already been replaced with a later model one and wasn't wired to work with the '84 wiring.<P>I was suprised the local parts stores around here don't carry the two speed motors for the '84's, and the dealer wanted about $250 for one, cripes!  <P>I've hooked up a switch from inside to turn it off and on.  I've found at rolling speeds I don't need it, but if I sit long enough the needle will slowly creep up.  I'd try to hook up some sort of fan just in case or get another motor if yours turns out to be bad.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 11-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-28-2000||08:06 PM||||unless you have an alternate switch the fan won't come on untill 235F. Acording to my notes 84 4 cyl was the only one with a 2 speed fan and only on AC cars. ||||reg||1
